The "AI Platform on EKS" project deploys the following third-party software. This
file records attribution and licensing.

This repository does NOT vendor (copy in) any third-party source. Everything
below is **deployed or fetched at runtime** — components this project pulls from
their official container registries, Helm repositories, or (for the Gateway API
Inference Extension CRDs) a pinned upstream Git tag at deploy time. This
repository does not redistribute them; it references them by image tag, chart
version, or Git tag. They remain under their own licenses, listed here for
attribution and operator awareness. Verify the exact license of the pinned
version before you rely on it.

================================================================================
SOFTWARE DEPLOYED / FETCHED AT RUNTIME (referenced, not redistributed)
================================================================================

** Gateway API Inference Extension (CRDs) — https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api-inference-extension
   Fetched at sync time from a pinned tag (currently v1.5.0), NOT vendored:
   platform/services/inference-gateway/kustomization.yaml references
   `.../config/crd?ref=v1.5.0`; ArgoCD runs kustomize build to install the CRDs
   (group inference.networking.x-k8s.io / inference.networking.k8s.io).
   Copyright The Kubernetes Authors. License: Apache-2.0.


Container images (pinned tags in platform/services/**):

  ** vLLM — https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
     image: vllm/vllm-openai (the serving engine behind all three tiers)
     License: Apache-2.0

  ** LiteLLM — https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm
     image: litellm/litellm:v1.81.9-stable.patch.1
     License: MIT

  ** Open WebUI — https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui
     image: ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.10.2
     License: Open WebUI License (BSD-3-Clause + branding-protection clause).
     ** NOT a standard OSI license. ** Removing/altering the "Open WebUI"
     branding is a material breach for deployments over 50 users; deployments of
     50 or fewer users may rebrand. Operators who run this sample pull that image
     and are subject to these terms.

  ** Langfuse — https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse
     deployed via the langfuse Helm chart (observability/tracing)
     License: MIT for the core; some enterprise ("ee") features are under a
     separate commercial license. This project deploys the OSS core (no "ee"
     feature is enabled by default).

  ** oauth2-proxy — https://github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy
     image: quay.io/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy:v7.7.1
     License: MIT

  ** curl (container) — https://github.com/curl/curl-container ; https://curl.se
     image: curlimages/curl (health/probe helpers)
     License: curl license (MIT/X-style)

Helm charts / platform components (pulled at deploy time):

  ** NVIDIA GPU Operator — https://github.com/NVIDIA/gpu-operator          License: Apache-2.0
  ** Argo CD (argo-helm) — https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd             License: Apache-2.0
  ** KRO (Kube Resource Orchestrator) — https://github.com/kro-run/kro     License: Apache-2.0
  ** Karpenter — https://github.com/aws/karpenter-provider-aws             License: Apache-2.0
  ** llm-d (llm-d-router-standalone) — https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d      License: Apache-2.0
  ** AWS EKS Blueprints Addons — https://github.com/aws-ia/terraform-aws-eks-blueprints-addons  License: Apache-2.0

Infrastructure baseline:

